TITLE:: SPFreqScope
summary:: the server's frequency scope, in ServerPanel's colours, with a frequency and dB grid
categories:: Libraries>ServerPanel
related:: Classes/SPScope, Classes/ServerPanel, Classes/FreqScope, Classes/FreqScopeView

DESCRIPTION::
What code::s.freqscope:: opens, drawn the way link::Classes/ServerPanel:: is. The grid has the frequencies (20, 50, 100 ... on a logarithmic scale, every kHz on a linear one) and the dB, 0 at the top. Point at the spectrum and the line along the bottom reads out the frequency, the nearest note with its cents, and the level.

What it changes against the stock one:
list::
## it reads a stereo bus: left and right summed, or one of them (the stock scope reads one channel);
## the fft size is free (2048, 4096, 8192), and the level stays the same at every size: a sine at -6 dBFS reads -6.4 to -6.7 dB at all three (measured 2026-11-05);
## the window resizes, and the spectrum stays on its grid at any width: a tone lands on its frequency to the bin in every mode and size (measured 2026-11-05, 100 Hz to 15 kHz).
::

There is one per server: asking again brings the open window to the front. ServerPanel's code::f:: key and its options menu open it. It survives cmd + period and a reboot, and frees its synth and scope buffer when it closes. It needs a server on this machine (shared memory).

code::
s.boot;
SPFreqScope(s);                  // the main out, left and right summed
SPFreqScope(s).source = 1;       // left only (2: right)
SPFreqScope(s).freqMode = 0;     // 0 linear, 1 logarithmic
SPFreqScope(s).dbRange = 72;     // how far down the bottom of the grid is
SPFreqScope(s).fftSize = 8192;   // finer at the bottom, slower to move
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
The frequency scope of a server, opened if it is not.
ARGUMENT:: server
A link::Classes/Server::; code::Server.default:: when nil.
RETURNS:: an SPFreqScope

METHOD:: synthDef
The analysis, named code::sp_freqscope0:: (linear) or code::sp_freqscope1:: (logarithmic).
ARGUMENT:: mode
0 or 1.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/SynthDef::

METHOD:: fftSizes
The sizes the window offers.

METHOD:: dbRanges
The ranges the window offers.

METHOD:: frames
How many points one sweep of the spectrum is drawn with: 2048, enough for a window up to 2048 pixels wide.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: inBus
The first of the two busses analysed.

METHOD:: source
0 both channels summed (halved), 1 the left, 2 the right.

METHOD:: freqMode
0 linear, 1 logarithmic.

METHOD:: dbRange
How many dB the height of the grid covers.

METHOD:: fftSize
The fft size, a power of two.

METHOD:: freqToX
Where a frequency is across the width.
ARGUMENT:: f
In Hz.
RETURNS:: 0 at the left edge, 1 at the right

METHOD:: xToFreq
The other way round.
ARGUMENT:: p
0 to 1.
RETURNS:: a frequency in Hz

METHOD:: nyquist
Half the server's sample rate.

METHOD:: running
Whether the scope runs. Paused, it has no synth on the server.

METHOD:: front
Bring the window to the front.

METHOD:: close
Close the window, freeing the synth and the scope buffer.

METHOD:: isOpen
Whether the window is up.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/Boolean::
